; PCP-I descriptor template for the AMD64 MiniOS optical image.
; It contains no boot code or filesystem payload. RIF emits the boot image;
; the ISO producer appends path tables, the root directory and files.
;
; PADDING provides ISO LBAs 0..15 (the system area). The RAW image contains
; only LBAs 16..19: the primary descriptor, boot record, descriptor
; terminator, and the El Torito validation/default-entry area.

MAGIC "pcpi"
VERSION 1
ENDIANNESS 1
BITORDER 1
SIGNATURE "MiniOS AMD64 ISO descriptor template"
PADDING 32768

@RAW

; LBA 16: ISO-9660 primary volume descriptor.
01 43 44 30 30 31 01 00
ZERO 72
; Volume-space-size, filled after the final image layout is known.
[8]
; Volume set size, sequence, logical block size and path-table metadata.
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 01
01 00 00 01
00 08 08 00
0A 00 00 00 00 00 00 0A
15 00 00 00
ZERO 4
00 00 00 16
ZERO 4
; Root-directory record, filled after the final directory layout is known.
[34]
ZERO 1886

; LBA 17: El Torito boot-record descriptor.
00 43 44 30 30 31 01
45 4C 20 54 4F 52 49 54 4F 20 53 50 45 43 49 46 49 43 41 54 49 4F 4E
ZERO 9
52 49 46 20 4D 49 4E 49 4F 53 20 42 4F 4F 54 20 43 41 54 41 4C 4F 47 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20
; The catalog remains at LBA 19, so its El Torito pointer is static.
13 00 00 00
ZERO 16
ZERO 1957

; LBA 18: volume-descriptor set terminator.
FF 43 44 30 30 31 01 00
ZERO 2040

; LBA 19: El Torito validation entry and default-entry hole. The ISO
; producer rewrites the validation entry and boot entry deterministically.
01 00 00 00 52 49 46 20 4D 69 6E 69 4F 53 20 45 6C 20 54 6F 72 69 74 6F 00 00 00 00 42 18 55 AA
[16]
ZERO 2000
@END
